//! The SILK pitch, LTP and excitation tables.
//!
//! These are the normative tables of RFC 6716 section 4.2 (the SILK layer),
//! reshaped into Zig arrays. Nothing here is derived: every number is a
//! coefficient, a cumulative probability or a codebook entry that the decoder
//! indexes straight out of the bitstream, so a table is behaviour.
//!
//! Generated once from the reference layout and then frozen; the array shapes
//! are what the indexing code in `opus_silk*.zig` relies on. Laid out
//! compactly on purpose: `zig fmt` would expand these to thousands of lines
//! with one number per line, which is why this generated data is not formatted.

